    "md5": "5fe774b4dcbc9e0513cd2787bf599aeb",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1872,
    "chunk_text": "Union Assurance expands emotional well-being programme islandwide\n\nUnion Assurance PLC is expanding the reach of its emotional well-being initiative \u2018Piripun Parapurak, Surakina Mehewarak\u2019, beyond Colombo, as part of its commitment to supporting the students across Sri Lanka.\n\nThe latest programme was held at Pushpadana Girls\u2019 College in Kandy, engaging over 300 students and marking another step in the initiative\u2019s journey to make emotional well-being awareness and support more accessible to students, equipping them to navigate the challenges of modern life.\n\nLaunched in 2025, Piripun Parapurak, Surakina Mehewarak was introduced to help schoolchildren build positive mindsets and strengthen their emotional well-being.\n\nThe initiative initially engaged the students across several schools in Colombo through expert-led discussions on emotional awareness, managing academic pressures and the impact of digital screens on personal development.\n\nBuilding on its long-term vision, Union Assurance has now entered the second phase of the programme, extending its reach to communities beyond Colombo and enabling more students across the country to access practical guidance and meaningful conversations on emotional well-being.\n\nThe interactive programme, delivered by qualified mental health practitioner, Counsellor and Psychotherapist Dr. Chaminda Weerasiriwardane, engaged the students in open conversations and practical exercises addressing some of the key challenges faced by the students today, including examination-related stress, academic pressures and the growing impact of digital screen dependency.\n\nThrough relatable scenarios, guided discussions and practical coping techniques, the students were encouraged to better understand their emotions, respond to challenges positively and develop healthier habits that support their overall well-being."
