    "chunk_size_bytes": 1870,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka and T\u00fcrkiye reaffirm commitment to strengthening bilateral relations\n\nLabour Minister and Finance and Planning Deputy Minister Dr. Anil Jayantha Fernando reaffirmed Sri Lanka\u2019s commitment to further strengthening bilateral relations with the Republic of T\u00fcrkiye, at the celebration of the 103rd anniversary of the Proclamation of the Republic of T\u00fcrkiye, held on October 29, 2026.\n\nSpeaking as the chief guest at the event, Dr. Fernando extended warm congratulations to President Recep Tayyip Erdo\u011fan and the government and people of T\u00fcrkiye on behalf of President Anura Kumara Dissanayake, the government and people of Sri Lanka.\n\nHe highlighted the long-standing friendship between Sri Lanka and T\u00fcrkiye, noting that although formal diplomatic relations were established in 1948, the historical connections between the two countries date back centuries through trade networks linking Asia, Europe and the Indian Ocean region.\n\nDr. Fernando recalled T\u00fcrkiye\u2019s swift and compassionate assistance to Sri Lanka following the devastating Indian Ocean tsunami in 2004 and its continued support during Sri Lanka\u2019s economic recovery.\n\nHe also expressed appreciation for T\u00fcrkiye\u2019s consideration of support for reconstruction following Cyclone Dithwah. In turn, Sri Lanka stood in solidarity with T\u00fcrkiye following the devastating earthquakes of 2023, reflecting the mutual understanding and solidarity between the two nations.\n\nEmphasising the potential for further economic cooperation, Dr. Fernando identified trade, investment, tourism, employment, renewable energy, hospitality and tourism, agro-processing, textiles and maritime logistics as key areas for collaboration. He encouraged Turkish investors and enterprises to explore opportunities in Sri Lanka, including those available through the Colombo Port City and dedicated investment zones."
