    "md5": "62d2b4c7470f07589b0038a4591f3fc0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1585,
    "chunk_text": "Government to reduce taxes further, says President\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake has announced that the government plans to introduce further reductions in certain taxes in the upcoming Budget, while ensuring that state revenue targets are maintained.\n\nSpeaking on the country\u2019s economic performance, the President said the government had achieved its revenue targets without introducing any new taxes since assuming office.\n\n\u201cWe have not imposed any new taxes since coming to power. In fact, we have significantly reduced some existing taxes. We will reduce certain taxes further in the upcoming Budget,\u201d he said.\n\nThe President emphasised that the proposed tax reductions would be implemented without compromising the government\u2019s revenue targets.\n\nHe noted that previous administrations had frequently failed to achieve their projected revenue targets, with actual collections often reaching only around 90% of the expected amounts.\n\nHowever, he said the current government had managed to exceed its revenue expectations while maintaining a primary budget surplus.\n\nAccording to the President, maintaining a primary budget surplus is essential to reducing the country\u2019s debt burden over time and strengthening its economic stability.\n\nHe also acknowledged the economic challenges faced by the public, particularly the impact of rising inflation on household expenses.\n\nThe President noted that increasing prices of goods and services had placed additional financial pressure on households, underscoring the need to provide relief while maintaining fiscal discipline."
