    "chunk_text": "Thousands of police officers were deployed across France to deal with the demonstrations, and officers fired tear gas at demonstrators in some cities.\n\nThere were more than 500 arrests after clashes in Toulouse, Lyon and Marseille.\n\nProtests also took place in Italy, with some clashes between police and demonstrators in Rome and Turin.\n\nIn Portugal, police moved to clear a new tent camp assembled after thousands marched to protest against a rental bill that they argue could worsen a housing crisis in the country, where house prices have more than doubled over the past decade.\n\nMostly young protesters have recently taken to the streets in a swathe of European nations: France, Belgium, Ireland, Spain, Portugal, Italy, Greece, Serbia and Albania.\n\nWhile the specific demands vary from country to country, the protesters have largely focused on cost-of-living issues, such as access to housing, the quality of education and cuts to public services."
