    "md5": "4c5355fd0a4b73e1a8d3048981770063",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1545,
    "chunk_text": "Naval, fishing communities warned against venturing into deep sea as cyclone Murasu intensifies\n\nColombo, Nov. 1 (Daily Mirror) - The Department of Meteorology has issued a red warning for strong winds and rough seas, advising naval personnel and fishing communities to refrain from venturing into deep-sea areas bounded by 10\u00b0N\u201315\u00b0N and 80\u00b0E\u201390\u00b0E until further notice, following the intensification of a deep depression in the Southeast Bay of Bengal into Cyclone Murasu.\n\nAccording to the Department, Cyclone Murasu was located near latitude 12.1\u00b0N and longitude 85.3\u00b0E at around 11.30 a.m. on November 1, 2026.\n\nThe cyclone is expected to move west-northwestwards and further intensify into a Severe Cyclonic Storm over the West-Central Bay of Bengal by the morning of November 2. It is then likely to move northwestwards before crossing the Andhra Pradesh coast in India as a Severe Cyclonic Storm between midnight on November 2 and the early hours of November 3, 2026.\n\nThe Department warned that wind speeds over the affected sea areas could reach 70\u201380 kmph at times, accompanied by heavy thundershowers. Sea conditions along the coastal belt stretching from Mannar to Trincomalee, via Kankesanthurai, are also expected to become very rough.\n\nIn view of the deteriorating weather conditions, naval and fishing communities have been strongly advised not to venture into the identified deep-sea areas until further notice.\n\nThose already operating in the affected waters have been urged to move to safer locations without delay."
  },
