    "chunk_size_bytes": 960,
    "chunk_text": "South Korean national arrested with cocaine worth Rs. 49.4 million at BIA\n\nColombo, Nov. 1 (Daily Mirror) - A 64-year-old South Korean national was arrested by officers of the Airport Police Narcotics Bureau at the Bandaranaike International Airport (BIA), Katunayake, while attempting to collect a suitcase containing cocaine worth approximately Rs. 49.44 million, police said.\n\nThe suspect, a carpenter by profession, had arrived at the airport on the afternoon of November 1 to collect the missing suitcase containing the narcotics.\n\nPolice said the suspect travelled from Tabuk Airport in Saudi Arabia to Dubai on October 26 before arriving in Sri Lanka aboard Flydubai flight FZ-579.\n\nThe suitcase containing the cocaine had not been loaded onto the flight on which he travelled to Sri Lanka and was subsequently sent to Katunayake Airport on another flight.\n\nPolice said the Inspector General of Police (IGP) received intelligence that led to the arrest."
