    "chunk_size_bytes": 691,
    "chunk_text": "President pays final respects to Lal Wijenayake\n\nColombo, Nov. 1 (Daily Mirror) - President Anura Kumara Dissanayake has paid his final respects to veteran left-wing political activist and senior lawyer Lal Wijenayake, who passed away on October 31.\n\nThe President visited a private funeral parlour in Kandy this afternoon (01), where the remains of the late lawyer are lying, to pay his last respects.\n\nDuring the visit, President Dissanayake also conveyed his heartfelt condolences to the bereaved family.\n\nWijenayake who was a senior member of the National People\u2019s Power (NPP) and served on its Executive Committee, was a prominent figure in Sri Lanka\u2019s left-wing political movement."
