    "md5": "46fd5ae4b20b8ab3d902bdd14f81041e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1481,
    "chunk_text": "Sunshine Holdings records strong growth in 1HFY27 with revenue up 24.4% and PAT rising 44.3%\n\nDiversified Sri Lankan conglomerate Sunshine Holdings PLC (CSE: SUN) reported strong top-line and bottom-line growth during the six months ended 30 September 2026 (1HFY27), recording a consolidated revenue of Rs. 40.2 billion, an increase of 24.4% year-on-year (YoY). The Group\u2019s profit after tax (PAT) increased by 44.3% YoY to Rs. 3.7 billion, supported by the resilience of the Group\u2019s diversified portfolio across Healthcare, Consumer and Agribusiness\n\nHealthcare remained the largest contributor to Group revenue, accounting for 49% of the total, followed by Consumer at 37% and Agribusiness at 14%. The Group\u2019s gross profit increased by 11.7% YoY to Rs. 11.5 billion, while its gross profit margin stood at 28.7%, compared to 31.9% in the corresponding period last year, primarily reflecting regulated pharmaceutical price reductions and the impact of a weaker rupee on the Healthcare sector.\n\nGroup earnings before interest and taxes (EBIT) increased by 10.5% YoY to Rs. 6.1 billion, while the EBIT margin stood at 15.1%, compared to 17% in 1HFY26. Higher net finance income and a lower effective tax rate supported the Group\u2019s profitability, with the PAT margin improving to 9.2% from 8% in the previous year. The Group also recorded stronger second-quarter momentum, with revenue increasing by 32% YoY to Rs. 21.6 billion and PAT growing by 82.4% YoY to Rs. 2.3 billion."
  },
