    "chunk_size_bytes": 1001,
    "chunk_text": "CIABOC challenges bail for Rakitha Rajapakshe, two others in Harak Kata case\n\nThe Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption (CIABOC) has filed a revision petition in the Colombo High Court seeking to overturn the Colombo Magistrate\u2019s Court\u2019s decision to grant bail to three suspects, including Rakitha Rajapakshe, in a bribery case involving the wife of Nandun Chinthaka Wickramaratne, alias \u2018Harak Kata\u2019.\n\nThe petition was scheduled to be taken up by the Colombo High Court on Friday.\n\nThe three suspects, Rakitha Rajapakshe, Charitha Abeysinghe and Waruna Handige Aruna Chathuranga, had been remanded over allegations of accepting a bribe from Wickramaratne\u2019s wife before the Magistrate\u2019s Court granted them bail.\n\nAccording to CIABOC, the allegations relate to Rs. 120 million allegedly demanded and obtained from the wife of the suspected organised criminal to facilitate assistance.\n\nRakitha Rajapakshe is the son of former Justice Minister Wijeyadasa Rajapakshe."
