    "chunk_text": "\"When you see that video, it's a jarring thing,\" Florida Governor Ron DeSantis told reporters at a news conference after the crash. \"It's like a missile coming down, and a massive explosion, debris going everywhere.\"\n\nIt is not yet clear who was aboard the jet when it crashed. DeSantis said \"as of now, we don't have any reports of anyone who was on the ground...who was killed or injured\".\n\n\"Please join me in praying for the families and loved ones of those we lost,\" Duffy added.\n\nPalm Beach County Fire Rescue has declared a \"mass casualty incident\".\n\nThe Palm Beach County Sheriff's Office said the crash happened on Military Trail, a six-lane road that features businesses and eateries.\n\nAt a news conference, DeSantis and local officials said that 600 local residents were being evacuated from a nearby trailer-park community.\n\nThe impact of the crash caused considerable damage to local infrastructure, including its water lines, they said, and it would be at least 30 days before the road re-opened.\n\nThunderstorms had been reported in the area at the time of the crash, and it was heavily raining as the news conference was held.\n\nTrump had been at Mar-a-Lago on Sunday morning, and departed from an airport nearby on Air Force One about an hour before the crash."
