    "chunk_size_bytes": 1622,
    "chunk_text": "SLASSCOM leads five-day business mission to Kenya\n\nThe Sri Lanka Association for Software and Services Companies (SLASSCOM) concluded a five-day business delegation to Nairobi recently , connecting Sri Lankan companies with Kenyan institutions, business leaders and prospective commercial partners.\n\nLed by Sampath Jayasundara, Chairperson of SLASSCOM, the delegation brought together senior representatives from Sri Lankan technology and business services companies to assess market opportunities, showcase local industry capabilities and explore avenues for export growth, investment and cross-border collaboration.\n\nThe mission included engagements across Kenya\u2019s public sector, private sector, financial services and technology ecosystem. The delegation engaged with a diverse range of organisations, including Bouer Limited, Invest Kenya, the Kenya National Chamber of Commerce and Industry, Equity Bank, the Murang\u2019a County Government, TESPOK, CPF Cooperative Pension Fund and Cisco. A meeting with Irungu Kang\u2019ata, Governor of Murang\u2019a County, was among the mission\u2019s public-sector engagements.\n\nThe range of stakeholders provided an opportunity to explore potential areas of demand across financial services, enterprise technology, digital transformation and business process management.\n\nThe mission also had the Sri Lanka delegation participating in the Sri Lanka Expo Breakfast Meeting organized by the embassy of Sri Lanka in Kenya to promote the Expo 2027 happening in Colombo, which brought Sri Lankan and Kenyan business leaders together to discuss trade, investment and partnership opportunities."
