    "chunk_size_bytes": 1051,
    "chunk_text": "The commission's findings have generated damaging headlines for City, while the club's response has been uncompromising. Both sides have committed themselves publicly to their positions, leaving little room for compromise.\u00a0 I've been in meetings where executives are so convinced of their position that even discussing alternatives feels disloyal. Advisers can become caught up in that confidence too, making it harder to raise uncomfortable questions.\n\nI have also sat in rooms with clients who listen intently when their lawyers speak but show considerably less interest when communications advisers raise concerns. Legal proceedings have established rules and outcomes. Public opinion is less predictable, and a favourable judgement does not necessarily restore confidence. Manchester City may succeed in its appeal, or the commission's findings may stand. The Premier League also has its credibility as a regulator at stake. Whatever the outcome, both organisations will have to contend with how the dispute has shaped public perceptions of them."
