    "chunk_size_bytes": 1970,
    "chunk_text": "Netanyahu pressing Trump to strike Iran immediately after midterms - Axios\n\nIRAN - Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu is pressing US President Donald Trump to strike Iran immediately after Tuesday's midterm elections, but Trump wants to let negotiations play out for now, Axios reported Sunday, citing an Israeli and a US source.\n\nThe two leaders had a candid phone call Saturday about the state of US negotiations with Iran and how quickly to return to combat, according to the report.\n\nThe Israeli source described the call as \"tough,\" while the US source called it \"direct.\"\n\nTrump is pursuing diplomatic efforts to restart negotiations with Tehran while preparing for a possible resumption of major military operations after the November 3 elections, according to the report.\n\nUS Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Saturday that Trump had not decided whether to launch further strikes against Iran and preferred a diplomatic solution.\n\n\"He hasn't made a decision. I have no announcement in that regard with you today, and nor do we take any of it lightly,\" Rubio told reporters in Atlanta.\n\nTrump told reporters Saturday that negotiations with Iran were \"going fine\" and that he was not \"in much of a hurry,\" but said the United States still needed to \"take care\" of one or two Iranian nuclear sites.\n\n\"We can do that in 10 minutes. We have that planned. You can look at Pickaxe Mountain. We need to take care of that. We can do that very quickly,\" Trump said, referring to a suspected nuclear facility built into a mountain.\n\nUS Vice President JD Vance sent a letter last week to Mohsen Rezaei, secretary of Iran's Supreme National Security Council, about the possibility of restarting negotiations.\n\nRezaei said Saturday that he had received and read the letter but had not responded, according to Iranian state media.\n\n\"I read the letter. I haven't yet responded. Their tone has completely changed,\" Rezaei said in remarks broadcast on Iranian television."
