    "md5": "5c5dd65f41be65c302c223372bce4cd6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1972,
    "chunk_text": "SLT-Mobitel reaffirms commitment to Sri Lanka-US business ties\n\nExecutive Committee representation strengthens company\u2019s role in advancing bilateral business collaboration\n\nSLT-Mobitel has reaffirmed its commitment to strengthening Sri Lanka-US business relations, joining the Sri Lanka-USA Business Council (SLUSABC) of the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce in celebrating a decade of advancing bilateral business engagement.\n\nThe council marked its 10th anniversary at its Annual General Meeting (AGM) held recently, with SLT-Mobitel supporting the milestone occasion as a Silver Sponsor.\n\nThe company was represented at the AGM by Chief Marketing Officer Rohana Ellawala and Deputy General Manager Global Business Dhanushka Medagama.\n\nAdding to SLT-Mobitel\u2019s continued engagement with the council, Dhanushka Medagama was elected to its Executive Committee for the second consecutive year, reinforcing the company\u2019s role in supporting initiatives that foster stronger business connections between Sri Lanka and the United States.\n\nThe occasion was graced by the chief guest, Ambassador of the United States to Sri Lanka Eric Meyer, alongside distinguished representatives from the business community, government institutions and member organisations.\n\nEstablished under the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce as its 22nd\u00a0 business council, the SLUSABC has played an important role in facilitating business engagement, encouraging partnerships and creating opportunities for collaboration between the two countries.\n\nFor SLT-Mobitel, participation in the council extends beyond corporate representation, providing a platform to engage with the US business community, strengthen international networks and explore opportunities aligned with its global business ambitions.\n\nAs digital connectivity and technology continue to shape international commerce, such partnerships create avenues for collaboration that can support trade, investment and technology-led economic development."
