    "chunk_text": "British Council-HSBC Sri Lanka unveil Youth Connect initiative\n\nThe British Council, in partnership with HSBC Sri Lanka, has launched Youth Connect: Inclusive Economic Empowerment (IEE) \u2013 Green Pathways, a new initiative designed to support young people in Sri Lanka in accessing employment, entrepreneurship and leadership opportunities in Sri Lanka\u2019s emerging blue-green economy.\n\nImplemented by SEVANTHA Urban Resource Centre and Muslim Aid Sri Lanka, the project will support young people to explore pathways into employment and entrepreneurship while promoting inclusive and sustainable economic growth.\n\nThe event also featured a symbolic launch celebrating the partnership between the British Council and HSBC Sri Lanka. Representatives from both organisations came together for a commemorative photograph to mark the launch of the initiative and reaffirm their shared commitment to helping young people access opportunities within Sri Lanka\u2019s emerging blue-green economy.\n\nBritish Council Sri Lanka Country Director Clare Sears said, \u201cSri Lanka\u2019s young people have the talent, ambition and potential to drive Sri Lanka\u2019s blue-green future. Through this partnership with HSBC, we are helping them translate that potential into opportunity by building the skills, confidence and connections needed to thrive in a rapidly evolving economy.\u201d\n\nHSBC Sri Lanka CEO Mark Surgenor said, \u201cThrough Green Pathways, HSBC is pleased to provide practical support, including mentoring, enterprise guidance and financial capability development, to young people exploring Sri Lanka\u2019s blue-green economy.\u201d\n\nOver the coming months, the participants will access learning opportunities, mentoring, industry engagement and practical support to strengthen their readiness for employment and entrepreneurship. Particular emphasis will be placed on supporting young women, young people with disabilities and young people facing barriers to economic participation."
