    "chunk_text": "Fitch upgrades BOC\u2019s national rating by two notches to \u2018AA+(lka)\u2019\n\nFitch Ratings upgraded the National Long-Term Rating of Bank of Ceylon (BOC), Sri Lanka\u2019s largest banking institution, by two notches to \u2018AA+(lka)\u2019 from \u2018AA-(lka)\u2019 with a Stable Outlook. This move recognises the bank\u2019s financial resilience and strong presence in the domestic banking sector, according to BOC.\n\nThe upgrade follows Fitch\u2019s revision of Sri Lanka\u2019s Long-Term Local-Currency Issuer Default Rating to \u2018B-\u2019 from \u2018CCC+\u2019, with a Stable Outlook, on September 22, together with the subsequent recalibration of the country\u2019s national rating scale. The improved assessment reflects the changing credit environment and provides greater recognition of BOC\u2019s relative credit strength among domestic financial institutions.\n\nFitch has identified BOC\u2019s leading position in the domestic banking sector, extensive branch network, broad customer base and strong deposit position as key factors supporting the upgrade.\n\nFurthermore, the improvement in Sri Lanka\u2019s sovereign credit environment and the upgrade of BOC\u2019s operating environment assessment to \u2018b-\u2019 from \u2018ccc+\u2019 are expected to ease macroeconomic pressures and support the bank\u2019s overall credit profile.\n\nCommenting on the upgrade, BOC Chairman Kavinda de Zoysa described it as \u201can important recognition of the bank\u2019s financial strength, resilience and leadership in Sri Lanka\u2019s banking sector.\u201d\n\n\u201cThis achievement reinforces our commitment to a clear strategic direction, sound risk management, prudent financial stewardship and a continued focus on strengthening our capital position. These priorities remain central to building a stronger, more resilient and sustainable institution. As the \u2018Bankers to the Nation\u2019, we remain committed to supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s economic progress, empowering businesses and creating long-term value for our customers, stakeholders and the nation,\u201d he added."
