    "chunk_size_bytes": 1982,
    "chunk_text": "People\u2019s Bank rated above private banks after two-notch Fitch upgrade\n\nFitch Ratings upgraded People\u2019s Bank\u2019s National Long-Term Rating by two notches to \u2018AA+(lka)\u2019 from \u2018AA-(lka)\u2019 with a Stable Outlook, placing the state-owned lender ahead of all private sector commercial banks in Sri Lanka on Fitch\u2019s national rating scale, the bank claimed.\n\nWith the upgrade, People\u2019s Bank now jointly holds the highest National Long-Term Rating among domestic commercial banks, which the bank described as an important endorsement of its underlying strengths, extensive customer franchise and dominant position within Sri Lanka\u2019s banking industry.\n\nIn announcing the rating action, Fitch recognised the significantly stronger domestic franchise of People\u2019s Bank relative to large private sector banks, highlighting its market-leading customer reach, extensive branch network, strong deposit franchise and established market position, which provide significant advantages in funding strength and stability.\n\nThe upgrade follows Fitch\u2019s recalibration of Sri Lanka\u2019s national rating scale after the recent improvement in the country\u2019s sovereign credit rating. The bank credits this revision with enabling greater recognition of its distinctive competitive strengths and relative creditworthiness within the domestic banking sector.\n\nPeople\u2019s Bank Chairman Chandana Guniyangoda called the upgrade \u201ca strong recognition of the confidence and trust the institution has earned over six and a half decades.\u201d\n\n\u201cBeing rated above all private sector banks is particularly encouraging and reinforces the importance of combining our national development mandate with sound commercial banking principles, strong governance and financial discipline,\u201d he added.\n\nThe upgrade comes as the bank pursues a strategic transformation of its business model, with greater emphasis on commercial competitiveness, operational efficiency, customer-centricity and digital innovation."
