    "chunk_text": "The bank said lower impairment charges reflected improved credit quality, recovery efforts and favourable changes in economic assumptions. Refinements to its expected credit loss models also affected impairment assessments.\n\nTotal assets increased by Rs. 66.43 billion, or 22 percent, from end-December to Rs. 374.45 billion at September 30. Net loans and advances expanded 17 percent to Rs. 243.45 billion, while customer deposits grew 19 percent to Rs. 274.89 billion over the same period.\n\nThe gross Stage 3 loan ratio, a measure of impaired lending, declined to 3.67 percent from 4.62 percent at end-2025. The corresponding net ratio fell to 1.44 percent from 1.73 percent, with provision coverage at 60.87 percent.\n\nReturn on equity stood at 15.25 percent, while pre-tax return on assets was 1.83 percent.\n\nThe bank\u2019s Common Equity Tier 1 capital ratio was 14.34 percent, while its total capital ratio stood at 15.67 percent, above the respective regulatory minimums of 7 percent and 12.5 percent. Its all-currency liquidity coverage ratio was 138.98 percent, against the minimum requirement of 100 percent."
