    "chunk_size_bytes": 1473,
    "chunk_text": "In the meantime, Jaffna is also going through social and political changes. A nihilist culture including incidents of gang violence and misogynist attacks against women are rising; even though women are socially advancing with a larger share in higher education and white collar jobs. For most young men and women, job opportunities are few, and the availability of and the remuneration for wage labour are low.\n\nThe NPP Government got a solid mandate in Jaffna two years ago and they have to deliver some tangible changes in the years ahead. Providing housing and housing land in Jaffna for the landless who are mainly from the oppressed caste is a priority. But, given that almost all the land in the Jaffna peninsula is privately owned, the Government would have to purchase land and redistribute.\n\nJob opportunities and work, including regular employment is, what youth are looking for, which requires investment. Furthermore, labour needs to be organised as trade unions are almost non-existent with little bargaining power of workers including to create a suitable working culture. Trade union work in the seafood processing plants, the few state-owned factories and the large number of unorganised shops and small businesses is a need. Activists from the community, established trade unions and the Labour Department have a role to play in organising workers and promoting labour rights, in a society more or less expunged of a trade union culture over many decades."
