    "chunk_text": "Job opportunities and work, including regular employment is, what youth are looking for, which requires investment. Furthermore, labour needs to be organised as trade unions are almost non-existent with little bargaining power of workers including to create a suitable working culture. Trade union work in the seafood processing plants, the few state-owned factories and the large number of unorganised shops and small businesses is a need. Activists from the community, established trade unions and the Labour Department have a role to play in organising workers and promoting labour rights, in a society more or less expunged of a trade union culture over many decades.\n\nThere is much to draw from the legacy of trade union and co-operative organising. The strategy for addressing caste oppression and exclusion in Jaffna today must draw inspiration from the anti-caste struggles of the late 1960s, but begin with creating the spaces for the youth and women to organise themselves around their livelihoods."
