    "md5": "fd622a3c10d2d47a5c8848fd67e1304b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1881,
    "chunk_text": "Saudi  execution of Bangladeshi couple sparks global outrage\n\nVisitors need to respect the laws of any given\u00a0 country they visit or work in,\u00a0 just as its own citizens do\n\nBangladeshi government says it wasn\u2019t given prior notice of the executions and learnt of the event via news reports\n\nA major row has erupted over the execution of two Bangladeshi nationals, a man and a woman, in Saudi Arabia on October 14. Saudi Arabia\u2019s interior ministry said they were executed for committing an \u2018immoral act\u2019 inside a mosque.\n\nNo details of this \u2018immoral act\u2019 have been made clear. Some unconfirmed reports say it was kissing, while others claim it was adultery.\n\nBangladeshi government says it wasn\u2019t given prior notice of the executions and learnt of the event via news reports.\n\nWhat is clear is that they were sentenced to death under an Islamic Law called Ta\u2019zir, under which the judge has the discretion to decide on both offence and sentence.\n\nIt isn\u2019t even clear if this is a married couple. There has been a deluge of social media misinformation which makes it very hard to get a clear picture. Claims that it was a honeymoon couple have been refuted. Bogus social media pictures of an Egyptian couple \u2013 the husband kissing his pregnant wife\u2019s belly inside what looks like a mosque \u2013 are circulating, claiming to be images of the executed Bangladeshis.\n\nNow it looks as if the two, Nazrul Islam and Siti Akhtar, have been working in Saudi Arabia for some time. Their ages and marital status has not been confirmed. What is confirmed is that both were executed on Oct. 14 under Islamic law for committing an unspecified \u2018immoral act\u2019 inside a mosque. The general consensus is that it was a kiss.\n\nBangladesh has demanded an explanation. But the country has over three million workers in Saudi Arabia, and is not in a position to take any strong action."
  },
